From a25652664217b15e68f775807ad6d87ab39943a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Sam (local build)" <sam@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:27:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] dde-emu v1c: send dynamic 0xE6/0xFB/0xE8 and the
 pre-ign statics; stats v3

Car test 2 (v1b) still degraded DSC/ICM/EPS at ign +1.15 s. The DTCs name
missing dynamic messages; per f11_emu2_dsc.md (v1c_rank_after_emu2) v1c adds:

- 0xE6 L9 (DT_PT_2): CRC 1<ctr> 80 64 45 44 23 47, E2E K=0x04, every 200
  cycles, cycle%8 == 2
- 0xFB L5 4<ctr> 60 f1 ff (1000 cycles, %8 5), L7 F<ctr> ff 47 32 00 f0
  (40 cycles, %8 6), L9 1f 00 04 00 00 f3 ff ff (1000 cycles, %8 3;
  pre-ign 1f 00 ff 7f 00 f3 ff ff as the real DDE)
- 0xE8 L9 00 00 00 9a 29 f3 56 f0 (200 cycles, %8 3), L5 86 78 fe fe
  (1000 cycles, %8 0, only from ign +225 ms)
- pre-ign statics: 0x28 c1 b3-b5 c1 17 7c, 0x29 c3 b8 80 until 60 ms after
  the first 0x103

Counters 0..14, starting at 1 after each wake. Each frame has its own build
switch (EMU_DYN_E6/FB/E8, EMU_PREIGN). Placement is skip-when-unsure: a
per-cycle tracker follows every FR1 header after the cycle's first
reference; the minislot of our frame is predicted from the last dynamic
frame (minislot grid fitted on run 5, k = 4/5/5/6 minislots for 2-4/6/8/14
payload bytes) and the frame is only sent when every frame start since the
anchor is explained by a decoded header on the grid, re-checked just before
TX. Otherwise the cycle is skipped (reason counted) and retried 8 cycles
later. 0x5C/0x142/0x10A/0x68 stay out. 14-byte frames leave the TX SM one
word short; it is restarted (counted as parks), not a fault. v1b fault
behaviour unchanged.

Stats v3 (192 bytes, first 128 = v2): sent/skip per PDU, skip reasons,
defers, last minislots, ign state, build flags, parks. Console: "emu: dyn".
